<title>UK: John Lewis UK store sales up 10.7% in week.</title>
<headline>John Lewis UK store sales up 10.7% in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said its UK department store sales rose 10.7 percent in the week to January 18 compared with the same week a year earlier.</p>
<p>In the 25 weeks to January 18, sales were up 12.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Total sales, including the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 9.8 percent in the week and were up 10.6 percent in the 25 week period.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
